## 2026-09-30 — #2020 attempt-1 tooling fixes, Chunk 1

Expected: the four failing event families would split between tooling and candidate behaviour, with the dashboard failure possibly caused by denied egress or WebKit.
Actual: all four were test-bed gaps, and none needed a candidate change. The README already listed three of them as "target prerequisites Chunk 1 prepares", but nothing ever prepared them.
Root cause: the soak harness's target contract (the README's prerequisites) was written as prose and never enforced. The seed and guest-setup were built and tested against their own outputs, not against the state the executors read. The first real guest was therefore the first consumer that checked the contract.
What changed: the new test/soak-repos-attach.test.js drives the real attach and startup sync over the seed and asserts the executors' preconditions. That turns the prose contract into a test at the producer/consumer boundary, and a regression there now fails in CI instead of in a 2-hour guest run.
Critic: 0 blocking. It caught an opaque refusal: setup reported a bare status while the cause sat in the discarded body. Fixed in the next commit.
Surprise: the wizard's Skip route refuses a loginless install (ADMIN_REQUIRED). Only Finish with noLogin works, and it also sets projectsDir, which closed setup item (b) for free.
